    "lines": [
      "Novelty That Resembles the Past asks whether the new can arrive in a familiar shape.",
      "It studies how language models judge unfamiliar contributions without confusing novelty with rarity or value.",
      "The book examines familiarity bias, semantic smoothing, and distinctions lost in representation."
